                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_496">Sheen, Surrey.
                        Charterhouse of Jesus of Bethlehem</orgName><p>Colophon (fol. 146r):
                        'Finito libro sit laus et gloria christo. Solvite nunc mentem pro W. H. ad
                        omnipotentem. De vita christi libro finis datur isti. Porro lactabit,
                        solidos quasi pane cibalis [sic]. De Bethlem [sic] pratum, dedit hos Iesu
                        tibi flores. Post hunc ergo statum, reddas sibi semper honorem' of M.
                        Deanesly, Lollard Bible, p. 325 (letter of J. P. Gibson in
                        C.V.L.).</p><p>The MS. is prefaced by a colophon which records the MS. was
                        produced at the Carthusian Charterhouse at Sheen by William Mede (d. 1474):
                        'Speculum deuotorum. et est Liber domus Ihesu de bethleem ordinis
                        cartusiensis de shene et nomen scriptoris Willelmus plenus
                     amoris.'</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Moore 137.</provenance>
               </history>
